settings.error.read_settings:
Try Omarchy cannot read its settings:

{error}

Fix or delete the file, then open the settings again.

recovery.backup.done:
Backup saved to:

{path}

It contains personal guest files and is not encrypted. Keep it private.

recovery.restore.confirm:
Restore this backup into a new folder?

{path}

Your current installation and shortcuts will stay unchanged. Only restore backups you trust.

recovery.restore.done:
Restored to:

{path}

Open Start Omarchy in that folder to use this copy, or Settings to review it first. Sign-in launch is off for the restored copy; enable it in Settings if wanted. Your original installation and shortcuts are unchanged.

recovery.restore.done_no_shortcuts:
Your data was restored to:

{path}

The startup shortcuts could not be created: {error}

You can start this copy with -dir pointing to its folder.

recovery.portable.done:
Portable copy created at:

{path}

Open Start Omarchy.cmd in that folder. Your original installation was kept.

move.confirm:
Move this installation?

From: {from}
To: {to}

Close Omarchy first. Saved settings and files will be copied and verified. The original will be kept until you start the moved copy and choose Remove previous location in Settings.

move.done:
Try Omarchy moved to:

{moved}

Start it normally to check your files. After a successful boot, Settings can remove the retained original at:
{original}

move.cleanup.confirm:
Remove the retained original installation?

{original}

The moved installation at {moved} will be kept. Files changed in the original since the move will stop cleanup.

preferences.repair.confirm:
Try Omarchy cannot read {file}.

{error}

Restore these preferences to their defaults? The original file will be backed up first. Guest files and the VM disk will not be changed.

